From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deewsing <deewsing@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 16:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] sched/core: skip sched_balance_trigger in sched_tick when RT task is runnable

Upstream-Status: Pending

On a PREEMPT_RT kernel, CPU0 is the tick_do_timer_cpu and cannot stop
its periodic tick (nohz_idle). CPUs 1-3 (also nohz_idle) successfully
stop their tick for seconds when idle. CPUs 4-7 are nohz_full.

Every ~20th RT wakeup cycle (tick period 4ms / RT interval 200us = 20),
the tick_nohz_handler expiry and the hrtimer_wakeup expiry for the RT
thread both fall within the same hrtimer_interrupt on CPU0. Both timers
are processed sequentially by __hrtimer_run_queues.

When tick_nohz_handler runs after hrtimer_wakeup, it calls:
  tick_sched_handle -> update_process_times -> sched_tick ->
  sched_balance_trigger

Because the tick fired ~903us late (jiffies advanced), rq->next_balance
is in the past and sched_balance_trigger raises SCHED_SOFTIRQ and calls
nohz_balancer_kick, which sends IPIs to all other CPUs. With all 8 CPUs
waking their RT threads simultaneously (thundering herd), this causes
~146us of additional hardirq latency on CPU0 while the RT thread is
already enqueued and waiting to run.

CPUs 1-3 are not affected because their tick is stopped for ~1.7 seconds
when idle, so tick_nohz_handler is never expired when their RT wakeup
fires. CPUs 4-7 are nohz_full and also unaffected.

Fix by skipping sched_balance_trigger in sched_tick when an RT or DL
task is runnable on this CPU. The RT task needs to run immediately;
triggering a load balance softirq and sending IPIs at this point only
adds latency without benefit. Load balancing will happen naturally once
the RT task sleeps and the CPU goes idle again via sched_balance_newidle.

Observed on IQ9075-EVK (SA8775P / Lemans, Cortex-A78C):
  cyclictest -a -t -m -p90 -i200 -h400 --spike 150 -b 151 --tracemark
  CPU0 hit 153us latency every ~20 cycles due to tick+RT timer collision.

Fixes: RT latency spikes on IQ9075-EVK (SEAPATH hypervisor port)
Signed-off-by: deewsing <deewsing@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 kernel/sched/core.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/core.c b/kernel/sched/core.c
index 582c3847f483..3079648c15da 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/core.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c
@@ -5618,10 +5618,26 @@ void sched_tick(void)
 	perf_event_task_tick();

 	if (donor->flags & PF_WQ_WORKER)
 		wq_worker_tick(donor);

+	/*
+	 * Skip load balance trigger when an RT or DL task is runnable.
+	 *
+	 * On nohz_idle CPUs that are also tick_do_timer_cpu (e.g. CPU0),
+	 * the periodic tick fires in the same hrtimer_interrupt as the RT
+	 * wakeup timer every N cycles (tick_period / rt_interval). When
+	 * sched_balance_trigger runs here it raises SCHED_SOFTIRQ and sends
+	 * nohz balancer IPIs while the RT task is already enqueued, adding
+	 * ~146us of hardirq latency before the RT task can run.
+	 *
+	 * Load balancing will occur naturally via sched_balance_newidle once
+	 * the RT task sleeps and the CPU returns to idle.
+	 */
+	if (rq->rt.rt_nr_running || rq->dl.dl_nr_running)
+		return;
+
 	if (!scx_switched_all()) {
 		rq->idle_balance = idle_cpu(cpu);
 		sched_balance_trigger(rq);
 	}
 }
